            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86145",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "pcre2: PCRE2: Out-of-bounds write allows arbitrary code execution via crafted regular expressions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "PCRE2 before 10.48 allows a pcre2_dfa_match out-of-bounds write because reuse of a cached workspace block, in a recursive DFA matching workspace, lacks a size check (even though a newly allocated block, for the same purpose, does have a size check). This outcome requires an attacker-controlled regular expression, or a recursive pattern in conjunction with a small heap limit (this can be set through the API)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86145",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86145\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libpcre2-8-0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-86145](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86145)\nPCRE2 before 10.48 allows a pcre2_dfa_match out-of-bounds write because reuse of a cached workspace block, in a recursive DFA matching workspace, lacks a size check (even though a newly allocated block, for the same purpose, does have a size check). This outcome requires an attacker-controlled regular expression, or a recursive pattern in conjunction with a small heap limit (this can be set through the API).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-86145**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libpcre2-8-0||[CVE-2026-86145](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86145)|\n\nPCRE2 before 10.48 allows a pcre2_dfa_match out-of-bounds write because reuse of a cached workspace block, in a recursive DFA matching workspace, lacks a size check (even though a newly allocated block, for the same purpose, does have a size check). This outcome requires an attacker-controlled regular expression, or a recursive pattern in conjunction with a small heap limit (this can be set through the API)."
              },
